-- title:
--   Drinfeld quotient field model of the invariant supersingular chart (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=2$ (hypothesis `hq2`), $M'$ is a nonzero level with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$ (`hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`).
--
--   **The base.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`); write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. `W` is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$, and `hW` says that `W` consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`: the places $w$ that are rational, affine geometric, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')` lies in `ssJSet q κ`, that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero point killed by $q$. An element $s$ of `W` is distinguished. The hypothesis `hle` requires `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` — the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, itself generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for $d \mid M'$ — to be contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ (units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$). Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the source together with a surjective residue map onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and a degree-preserving map on places satisfying the order-transport clause. The hypothesis `hR₀` identifies this reduction with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Constants.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` is the trace of $A$ to $k_0$. An element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lies in $A$ (`hπ`), and `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` require $A_0$ to be a discrete valuation ring, Henselian, with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and with algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` requires every element of $A$ to be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Auxiliary constants: a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$ (`hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`); $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity (`hζ₀`); $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖtA`, `hϖt`), and $\varpi_t' \in A_0$ equal to $\varpi_t$ (`hϖt'`); an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b = \bot$ (`hKb`), carrying a valuation subring $A_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$ (`hAb`) and whose maximal ideal is generated by a non-zero $\varpi_b$ (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`); the tameness clause `htame`, that the image of $(\ell_g-1)/2$ is a unit of $A_0$; and $\xi \in k_0$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hξ`).
--
--   **The rigid level field and its chart.** $H_1$ is the intersection of `levelH q M'` with the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$ (`hH₁`); $K_\ell$ is the $k_0$-base change `laurentBaseChange k₀ (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)` of the function field of $X_{H_1}$ of level $q^2M'$ (`hKℓ`), equipped with its algebra and scalar-tower structures over $A_0$; $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ is non-zero and equals the coefficient embedding `coeffEmb k₀ jq` (`hjℓ`). The ring `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ` is the set of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$; $y$ is a maximal ideal of it (`hy`) containing the image of $\pi_0$ (`hϖy`). The supersingularity hypothesis `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`. The hypothesis `hover` identifies $y$ as the specialisation attached to $s$: for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in `R₀.integers`, which has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which `jq` does, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, and for every witness that `coeffEmb k₀ g` lies in $K_\ell$ and in the chart, and every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals `s.evalAt` of that $R_0$-residue, the chart element $g - c$ lies in $y$. The hypothesis `hOrbit` requires every maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same condition to be carried to $y$ by a level automorphism: there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` preserving the chart algebra and with $b \in y \iff \tau b \in y'$. Here `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` says that $\tau$ realises on $q$-expansions the action of the matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`: for all weight-$k$ modular forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, $g$ with non-zero series, and every $x \in K_\ell$ whose Laurent series is the corresponding quotient, and every embedding $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathtt{conjElemN } q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals that of $f\mid_k \mathtt{conjElemN } q\,\gamma^{-1}$. Finally `hjK`, `hjC` and `ha₀y` require `jqNModC k₀ q` $=$ `qExpand k₀ q (jqModC k₀)` to lie in $K_\ell$ and in the chart, and its difference with a given $a_0 \in A_0$ to lie in $y$.
--
--   **The rigid chart package.** $B_t$ is an $A_0$-subalgebra and $W_t$ a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hS1` (a long conjunction, summarised here) requires: the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$ and $K_\ell$ is the fraction field of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$, and $B_t/\pi_0$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t \cap k_0 = A_0$, $W_t$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, the ideal $y$ is the contraction of that maximal ideal to the chart, and $W_t$ is the corresponding localisation of $B_t$; for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A_0$ there is a surjection $\rho$ of $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring `CoordRing q` of that residue field (two-variable polynomials modulo `drinfeldPoly q − 1`) whose vanishing locus is the maximal ideal of $W_t$, compatible with residues of $A_0$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms through `hAction` at elements `(redQ q γ, c)` of `hSubgroup q` (the kernel of $(g,c) \mapsto \det g \cdot c^{q+1}$), with $c \ne 1$ for a non-trivial $\tau$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and with a companion automorphism realising $(1,c)$; the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B_t$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is reached from the centre of $W_t$ by some level automorphism; and an element of $B_t$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W_t$ after every such automorphism is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   Further numerical and dynamical data: $n \ge 1$ divides $q+1$ (`hn1`, `hnq`) and `hn` requires $n =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, namely `jWidthChar q (s.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M'))` divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`, the numerator being $12$ or $1$ according as that $j$-invariant vanishes or not, since $q = 2$; $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau_0$ with `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma_0^{-1}$, preserving $W_t$ (`hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`, `hτ₀`, `hτ₀W`); $m \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t'$ times a unit of $A_0$ (`hm1`, `hm`); $\zeta_c$ an $n$-th root of unity in the $\pi_0$-adic completion of $A_0$ with $\zeta_c^k - 1$ a unit for $0 < k < n$ (`hζc`, `hζcprim`); and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$. The hypothesis `hR7` (a long conjunction, summarised here) requires: $\tau_0$ acts on $B_t$ with exact order $n$, and every level automorphism preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power $\tau_0^k$, $k < n$; `ends` has $q+1$ members, is permuted by the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ that preserve $W_t$ and transitively so, each member is stabilised by $\tau_0$, and distinct members are separated by an element which is a unit in one and not in the other; there is a finite-type subalgebra $B_c$, stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, contained in every member of `ends`, of which each member is a localisation; a level automorphism carrying a member into $W_t$ preserves $W_t$; and each member $O$ of `ends` is a local Noetherian subring of $W_t$ containing the chart algebra, with $O \cap k_0 = A_0$ and with every element congruent to a constant, whose completion at its maximal ideal is identified by an isomorphism $\iota$ with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` of the completion of $A_0$ at $\pi_0^m$ (two-variable power series modulo $X_0X_1 - \pi_0^m$) in such a way that two elements $c_x, c_y$ of $O$ with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m \cdot \text{unit}$ correspond to units times the coordinates $U$ and $V$, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, the element `jqNModC k₀ q` $- a_0$ corresponding to a unit times $V^e$ with $e \ge 1$, and the action of $\tau_0$ corresponding to an automorphism $\theta_0$ with $\theta_0 U \equiv \zeta_c U$ and $\theta_0 V \equiv \zeta_c' V$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal, where $\zeta_c\zeta_c' = 1$; each such $O$ moreover comes with a valuation subring $W_x$ and a subalgebra $B_x$ of $K_\ell$ with prescribed integrality, invariance, centre and separation properties. A final clause of `hR7` requires that a valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ with $V \cap k_0 = A_0$, containing the chart algebra and with centre $y$ on it, either contain $B_t$ or dominate one of the members of `ends`.
--
--   The hypotheses `hR9` and `hR10` (summarised here) are separation clauses: an element of $B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ with $V \cap k_0 = A_0$ at which $\pi_0$ is a non-unit and at which no monic polynomial in $j_\ell$ over $A_0$ becomes a non-unit; and, for every maximal ideal $y''$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ which is not carried to $y$ by any level automorphism, an element of $B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring containing the chart whose centre pulls back to $y''$ along the automorphism in question.
--
--   **The descent data.** $G$ is the subgroup of the $k_0$-automorphism group of $K_\ell$ generated by all $\tau$ for which some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` (`hG`); $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`); $B_0$ is the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ whose elements are exactly the $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$ (`hB₀`); and $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`, and assuming `CoordRing q κ` is a domain, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho : B_0 \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the subfield of the Drinfeld function field `drinfeldFunctionField q κ` $=$ `FractionRing (CoordRing q κ)` fixed by the subgroup generated by `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at the elements $(1,\zeta)$ with $\zeta \in C_s$, such that:
--
--   (i) the cardinality of $C_s$ equals `placeWidthChar q M' s`;
--
--   (ii) the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal of $B_0$ generated by the image of $\pi_0$;
--
--   (iii) for every $a \in A_0$, the value $\rho(a)$ is the image, under the structure map of $\kappa$ into the quotient field, of the residue in $\kappa$ of $a$ viewed as an element of $A$;
--
--   (iv) every $z$ in `quotField q κ Cs` is a quotient of values of $\rho$: there are $g, h \in B_0$ with $\rho h \ne 0$ and $z \cdot \rho h = \rho g$;
--
--   (v) an element $z$ of `quotField q κ Cs` lies in the range of $\rho$ if and only if $z$, viewed in `drinfeldFunctionField q κ`, lies in the image of `CoordRing q κ`;
--
--   (vi) equivariance: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ`, every witness that `(redQ q γ, 1)` lies in `hSubgroup q`, and every $f \in B_0$ with $\tau f \in B_0$, the image of $\rho(\tau f)$ in `drinfeldFunctionField q κ` equals `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at `(redQ q γ, 1)` applied to the image of $\rho(f)$.
--
--   This is the identification, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ diamond frame at $q = 2$, of the special fibre of the supersingular affine chart descended to the $G$-invariants $B_0$ with a Drinfeld-curve quotient $\kappa[\mathrm{DL}]^{C_s}$ over the residue field of $A$, together with the level-equivariance of that identification and the computation of $\#C_s$ as the width character of the supersingular place $s$. It feeds the integral-closedness statement for the invariant quotient and the construction of the supersingular discrete valuation ring on the invariant affine chart in the same frame.
